From befbe6943c79492d8314ee1e09a60574c38d05e5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 11:24:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07402/11362] [outer-loop] REQ-ARC-FCP-5758: small-object-first
 click-reorder A/B vs the exp5757 selection gap (clean NULL, Missing-Verifier
 reframe)

Follows up REQ-ARC-FCP-5757, which localized Carnot's only residual single-action
ARC gap to SELECTION/RANKING of object clicks (bucket c: 6 action-6 clicks in-set +
frame-changing but ranked >=12; r11l x1, su15 x4).

Diagnosis (reproduced the gap frames, dumped per-object salience features): the
low-ranked winning clicks are consistently TINY objects (r11l rank-22 winner area=1;
su15's repeatedly-clicked winner area=1; r11l others area 4/12). The shipped default
salience area*(1+1/(1+global_color_px)) is AREA-DOMINATED, so a 1-pixel target loses
to large decorative regions. Honest nuance: the single-pixel winners are ALSO buried
under many equal-size rarer-colored pixels, so no monotonic-in-area formula surfaces
them -- part of the gap is a discriminating-SIGNAL absence, not a formula bug.

Fix: opt-in, gated-OFF-by-default reorder CARNOT_ARC_SMALL_OBJECT_FIRST=1
(arc_graph_explore._small_object_first_click_points): a SMALL band (area<=8, rarest
color first) tried before the proven salience order. Byte-identical when off; pure
reorder (no click added/dropped). Genuinely different from the two already-NULL
reorders (CARNOT_ARC_TIER_SCHEDULE medium-width, exp4556 learned candidate_router).

Live A/B (exp5758, 11-game roster, budget=200, no-LLM, per-game fixed seed): clean
NULL. Both arms bank 1 level (lp85, incidental; headroom present). r11l/su15 stay 0
in BOTH arms (r11l_su15_specifically_fixed=false, the decisive negative). Search
changes on 7/11 games but banks no extra level and actually gets cheaper (states
931->807, -13%, no regression). Offline rank-shift is a WASH (0/2 decisive games
reduce their low-rank count). adversarial_verify: 0 flags. Flag stays OFF; gap logged
as GAP-ARC-CLICK-SELECTION-5758 for a learned/goal-conditioned click discriminator.

